  "scope": "Complete integral transformation under all three printed alternatives: Hausdorff measurability of the finite real weight, almost-everywhere finite multiplicity, or measurability of the weighted source integrand. Prove equality of the actual integral graphs and integrability domains, including infinite values and undefined signed integrals. The numbered theorem retains m<=n; supporting proofs work in arbitrary ambient dimensions. Prove completed-Borel pullback on countable injective pieces without global target sigma-finiteness, measurable and countably measurable images, abstract cutoff laws and measurable existence, nonnegative and signed transformations, division by the actual positive Jacobian on the 3.2.4 selection, null-deficit recovery, finite-multiplicity weight recovery, and null inverse-image weight replacement. Two regressions exercise arbitrary weights without target measurability on empty and zero-dimensional sources.",
